    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 22-layer HfO2/SiO2 alternating stack on fused silica substrate for solar-blind UV bandpass filtering. Initialize all 22 layer thicknesses to the following values in nm from air to substrate: [57.29, 34.20, 36.06, 67.58, 24.38, 77.85, 92.06, 50.08, 24.74, 78.38, 49.64, 30.57, 22.93, 54.73, 63.11, 30.04, 38.67, 104.95, 82.26, 95.09, 38.40, 26.83]. Apply gradient-based thickness optimization with the following constraints: layers 1-9 and 15-22 are FIXED at initialization values; layers 10-14 (indices 10, 11, 12, 13, 14) are OPTIMIZABLE with perturbation bounds of ±0.5 nm from initialization. Evaluate transmittance at normal incidence across three wavelength bands: 255-280 nm (maximize), 300-700 nm (minimize), 700-1100 nm (minimize). Use composite target score weighting all three bands equally. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 255-280 nm, 300-700 nm, 700-1100 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 255–280 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: Transmittance in 300–700 nm; Transmittance in 700–1100 nm. manufacturing constraints: Maximum 30 layers; No metal layers; Only conventional depositable inorganic dielectric materials.",
